11. Source notes
This v2 plan is based on the PO-GUISE paper/repo notes, the PO-GUISE+ manuscript notes, Toyota-Smarthome dataset facts, and the previous planning document. Important source facts used:
Toyota-Smarthome is described as 16K RGB+D clips across 31 activity classes, performed by seniors in a smarthome.
PO-GUISE uses a clip-level class token and heatmap tokens; heatmaps guide pruning but do not by themselves provide per-person identity binding.
PO-GUISE+ adds object heatmaps and is detector-free at inference, but still predicts a clip-level driver action plus heatmaps, not multiple per-person ADL actions.
PO-GUISE/PO-GUISE+ edge results support efficient live deployment, but longer temporal context/time-action localization is identified as future work, not solved by the base architecture.
Operational rule: in code, import/reuse the repo dataset label map for the 31 Toyota classes. Do not hand-type class order into a new file unless you are copying it exactly from the repo and adding a unit test.